<p>Two sentences carry the whole design.</p>
<p><strong>Templates compile; content does not.</strong> A template is Rust. The compiler reads
it, type-checks it and puts it in the binary. A markdown document is data. The
built binary reads it at run time. The two sit on different clocks: a template
edit pays for a compile, a content edit does not.</p>
<p><strong>There is no backend.</strong> The output is files. Nothing runs at request time, so
any static file server can publish the result.</p>
<h2 id="what-it-is-for">What it is for</h2>
What it is for
<p>A documentation site, or any site whose content is markdown and whose shell is
a navigation tree. depoth gives you one configuration file, one navigation
declaration, compiled templates, and a build that writes HTML to a directory.
Navigation is declared once and yields the sidebar, the tab bar, the
breadcrumbs and the prev/next links, so they cannot disagree with each other.</p>
<p>It also prerenders partial navigation. Each route is written as a complete
document and again as a set of smaller trees, so a client with JavaScript can
replace only the part of the page that changed. Every page still works with
JavaScript off, because the document was never derived from the fragment.</p>
<h2 id="what-it-is-not-for">What it is not for</h2>
What it is not for
<p>Anything that needs compute when a visitor asks for a page. There is no request
handler, no session, no form endpoint and no database. An interactive API
playground needs a server to proxy requests, so depoth does not have one.</p>
<p>It also does not choose your CSS framework, your bundler or your JavaScript
toolchain. The framework proposes a pre-build command hook and stays out of
what you run in it. This site uses Tailwind; depoth does not know Tailwind
exists.</p>
<h2 id="maturity">Maturity</h2>
Maturity
<p>Early. The repository is at version 0.1.0 and contains the configuration
parser, the navigation model, the frontmatter splitter and the test harness.
The render pipeline, the command-line interface, the component library and
search are not written yet. Where a page below describes something that is not
built, it says so.</p>
<p>The predecessor is real, which is why the decisions are not guesses. The
Crystal depoth reached 0.2.0 with 315 specs and one 489-page production site.
Most of what you read here is inherited from it rather than invented here.</p>

