</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>pages</code></td>
<td>list of nodes</td>
<td>Optional.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>A tab with neither pages nor groups nor an <code>href</code> is an error: it is a control
that cannot go anywhere. A tab that is only an <code>href</code> is allowed and is the
normal way to put a link to a source repository in the tab bar.</p>
<h2 id="groups">Groups</h2>
Groups
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Key</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>group</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>required</td>
<td>The label.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>icon</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>none</td>
<td>Optional icon name.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>tag</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>none</td>
<td>A short badge beside the group name.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>root</code></td>
<td>slug</td>
<td>none</td>
<td>Clicking the group title opens this page.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>expanded</code></td>
<td>boolean</td>
<td><code>false</code></td>
<td>Whether a nested group starts open.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>pages</code></td>
<td>list of nodes</td>
<td>empty</td>
<td>The children.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>A nested group is an accordion and is closed unless <code>expanded</code> is set. A
top-level group is always open. That is Mintlify's rule and a good one: the
outermost level is a section heading, not a control.</p>
<p>A group's <code>root</code> page is placed before its children, which is the order a
reader meets them.</p>
<h2 id="pages">Pages</h2>
Pages
<p>An entry under <code>pages</code> is either a slug or a nested group. Nothing else. In
particular there is no external link here, because a link belongs to a tab or
to an anchor.</p>
<pre class="hl"><code class="language-yaml"><span class="hl-source hl-yaml"><span class="hl-string hl-unquoted hl-plain hl-out hl-yaml"><span class="hl-entity hl-name hl-tag hl-yaml">pages</span></span><span class="hl-punctuation hl-separator hl-key-value hl-mapping hl-yaml">:</span>
