</span></code></pre>
<h2 id="anchors">Anchors</h2>
Anchors
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Key</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>anchor</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>Required. The label.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>href</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>Required. External URL.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>icon</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>Optional icon name.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Anchors are shown on every page regardless of section.</p>
<h2 id="what-flattening-produces">What flattening produces</h2>
What flattening produces
<p>The tree is flattened once into a list of entries in reading order. Each entry
carries its slug, the tab it sits under, the trail of enclosing group names
outermost first, and its index in the whole order.</p>
<p>The trail is the breadcrumb. The index is the prev/next order. The sidebar is
the same walk, stopped at the current tab. <code>llms.txt</code> is the same list again.
One flatten, four readers.</p>
<h2 id="a-page-listed-twice-is-rejected">A page listed twice is rejected</h2>
A page listed twice is rejected
<p>Validation fails if any slug appears more than once in the flattened order.</p>
<p>Two sidebar entries for one page makes prev/next ambiguous — the reader can
arrive at the page from one position and leave from the other — and it makes
the active-state highlight flicker between the two entries. There is no answer
that is right, so the tree is refused instead.</p>
<h2 id="prevnext-stops-at-a-tab-boundary">Prev/next stops at a tab boundary</h2>
Prev/next stops at a tab boundary
<p>The page before and after a slug are its neighbours <strong>within its own tab</strong>. The
last page of a tab has no next page, even though another page follows it in the
flat order.</p>
<p>A tab is a section a reader chose to be in. Walking them out of it with a
&quot;Next&quot; button is a navigation they did not ask for, and it lands them somewhere
with a different sidebar and no way back along the trail they were following.
If the site has no tabs, every page is in the same <code>None</code> tab and prev/next
runs end to end.</p>

