<p>Four details there are load-bearing rather than decorative.</p>
<ul>
<li>The match is <code>~*</code> because header values are not the client's to normalise.</li>
<li><code>Vary</code> is mandatory. Several bodies share one URL, so a cache that saw a
fragment will otherwise hand it to the next visitor asking for a document.</li>
<li>A partial request that misses falls through to <code>@full</code> rather than to a 404,
because a route that exists only at a shallower depth should still answer.</li>
<li>The 404 page is deliberately not a <code>try_files</code> candidate. When it was, a
partial request for a missing page got a whole document back and the client
spliced a second navbar into the page.</li>
</ul>
<p>Redirects become exact-match <code>location</code> blocks, which nginx resolves before any
prefix location, so they cost nothing on the pages that are not redirects.</p>
<p>The <code>build</code> and <code>nginx</code> commands are not implemented in this repository yet;
they are prerender's, and depoth passes through to them.</p>

