<p>A depoth site is a Rust crate. There is no <code>depoth</code> binary to install on your
machine and no theme to download. You create a crate, add three dependencies,
and the crate builds your site.</p>
<h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
Requirements
<p>A Rust toolchain. The workspace declares a minimum of 1.97, which is what the
dependency tree requires: <code>oxc_parser</code> 0.153 asks for 1.97 and edition 2024,
and <code>comrak</code> 0.55 asks for 1.85.</p>
<p>Pin the toolchain for the project. <code>rsx</code> compiles templates in a procedural
macro, and its macro artifacts are not compatible across patch releases of
rustc. Two different rustc on <code>PATH</code> compile the host half and the target half
differently, which fails in a way that does not name the cause.</p>
