<p><code>depoth</code> reads the configuration, the navigation and the content. <code>rsx</code>
compiles your <code>.rsx</code> templates into the binary. <code>prerender</code> renders each route
as a document and as its partial trees, and writes them to disk.</p>
<h2 id="the-layout-of-a-site">The layout of a site</h2>
The layout of a site
<pre class="hl"><code class="language-text"><span class="hl-text hl-plain">my-site/
  Cargo.toml
  depoth.yaml      the site&#39;s identity, directories and navigation
  content/         markdown documents
  src/
    main.rs
    views/         .rsx templates, compiled into the binary
  assets/          stylesheets and scripts
  public/          copied verbatim
</span></code></pre>
<p><code>content</code>, <code>dist</code>, <code>public</code> and <code>assets</code> are the defaults. Every one of them is
a configuration key, so you can move them. See
<a href="/docs/configuration">Configuration</a>.</p>
<h2 id="building">Building</h2>
Building
<pre class="hl"><code class="language-sh"><span class="hl-source hl-shell hl-bash"><span class="hl-meta hl-function-call hl-shell"><span class="hl-variable hl-function hl-shell">cargo</span></span><span class="hl-meta hl-function-call hl-arguments hl-shell"> run<span class="hl-keyword hl-operator hl-end-of-options hl-shell"> --</span></span><span class="hl-meta hl-function-call hl-arguments hl-shell"> build</span>
</span></code></pre>
<p>The first build compiles every dependency and takes about 21 seconds on a cold
<code>target/</code>. After that a template edit rebuilds in about half a second, and a
content edit does not rebuild at all — it re-runs the binary you already have.
<a href="/docs/design-notes">Design notes</a> has the measurements.</p>
<p>The build command is not implemented in this repository yet; the crate today
carries the configuration parser, the navigation model and the frontmatter
splitter.</p>

